  "authoringNotes": {
    "status": "approximate corridor traced from OpenStreetMap (snapshot 2026-10-29) and checked against GSI 1974–1978 aerial photos (gazo1), the 1972–1975 and 1988–1991 1:25,000 topographic maps (今昔マップ on the web, dataset 会津) and the GSI DEM; GSI has no 1979–1990 aerial tiles (gazo2/gazo3/gazo4) for Aizu-Wakamatsu; not surveyed or native-qualified",
    "sprintRoute": "JNR Aizu-Wakamatsu Station plaza → Ōmachi-dōri (south) → Ōmachi-yotsukado → Nanokamachi-dōri (west) → prefectural road 59 (south) → Yonedai → Jōnan-dōri (east) → National Route 118 along the Nishi-demaru moat (north) → castle north street past Kita-demaru and the Fukushima Museum (east) → Tenneiji-machi → Iimoriyama-dōri (north) → Iimori 1-chōme lanes → Keizan forest road to Iimoriyama's south shoulder",
    "lapsReason": "Sprint: one lap with real start and finish; no return leg.",
    "finish": "Highest point of Iimoriyama reachable by road: the Keizan forest road (林道慶山線) where it crests the south shoulder and bends away south, ≈297 m by GSI DEM, level with the Byakkotai graves (≈297 m) and ≈175 m south of the 371 m summit. The castle keep is 2.85 km away on bearing 237°. The stone stairs and the slope conveyor are not used. Past the bend the track leaves Iimoriyama south-east into the Keizan hills.",
    "oneWay": "Ōmachi-dōri is driven southbound, its present one-way direction (OSM oneway=yes); the 1986 regulation is unconfirmed. Every other leg is two-way today.",
    "unconfirmed": "Public car access to the forest road in 1986 is unconfirmed: today it is a road under 3 m wide (GSI category 市区町村道等); it shows as a track on the 1974–1978 photos and as a light road on the 1988-revised map. The Iimori 1-chōme lanes are absent from the 1972–1975 map and 1974–1978 photos and present on the 1988-revised map.",
    "elevationsAndWidths": "Elevations from the GSI DEM (5 m and 1 m laser meshes), smoothed over 120 m in town and 40 m on the hill; not survey levels. Half-widths are game corridors: 4.2–5.6 m in town, 3.0 m in the lanes and 2.6 m on the forest road. That makes the forest road 5.2 m wide, against under 3 m in reality, because the compiler minimum is 2.5 m.",
    "musicCues": "Placeholder audio and hash. Cues: start at the JNR station; castle reveal turning north along the Nishi-demaru moat; turn north at Tenneiji-machi toward Iimoriyama; the climb from Iimori 1-chōme; the forest-road finale.",
    "pacing": "targetMs is an estimate, not a drive. A speed-profile model, with grip calibrated so the Tokyo draft averages 200 km/h, gives ≈153 s for computer cars and ≈162 s at 70% grip. 165 s is the good-driver target. maxTicks 9000 (300 s) leaves ≈135 s for slow cars.",
    "notForProfile": "Current RaceV1 accepts only 3 tracks and 5400 ticks. This input cannot be submitted to it.",
    "cornerGeometry": "Quadratic tangent trims in millimetres, not physical radii (the Tokyo convention). Town corners use 24–28 m trims. Outside corner fillets the centreline stays within 3 m of the OSM centreline; at fillets the offset reaches ≈6 m."
  },
